Australian Product Guide — Brand Conformity v34.1 exhaustive whole-site presentation release
Release date: 2026-08-18
Status: CURRENT only when this exact GitHub main SHA has Vercel READY and APG v34.1 Brand Conformity Certification = SUCCESS; otherwise treat as RELEASE CANDIDATE
Production source: GitHub main via Vercel
Canonical production domain: https://australianproductguide.au

Current platform: Brand Conformity v34.1 is the governing presentation layer over the observer-loop-free Brand Fidelity v32.5.1 baseline, Premium Theme v31.1, Premium Brand v30 and the maintained APG application/data stack. The architecture remains lightweight SSR-first Node with progressive enhancement. v34.1 changes presentation, Scout identity and release controls only; it does not change product-fit logic, catalogue data, retailer ranking, affiliate weighting, account/auth behaviour, analytics consent or privacy controls.

Approved palette contract: APG Blue #2563EB and APG Navy #0F172A lead the consumer experience, with white, Light Grey #F1F5F9 and Slate #64748B providing neutral surfaces and text hierarchy. APG Teal #06B6D4 is a restrained secondary accent. APG Green #10B981 is retained because it is part of the approved brand board, but v34.1 restricts it to genuine semantic success/verified cues rather than decorative legacy theming. Historical green/cyan families such as #047857/#ECFDF5/#A7F3D0 and #0891B2/#ECFEFF/#0E7490/#38BDF8 are not permitted as controlling visible decorative colours.

Yellow research treatment: the intentional MAINTAINED AUSTRALIAN RESEARCH band remains an approved high-attention trust exception using the recovered historical yellow family #FFD65B → #F4BB45 → #F2B348 with dark readable foreground treatment. Its catalogue/category/brand figures remain data-driven rather than release constants.

Whole-site conformity scope: v34.1 normalises remaining decorative legacy colour usage across shared navigation, mega-menu, homepage decision modules, category artwork variables, comparison/difference surfaces, account nudges, retailer states, evidence/success modules and Scout surfaces. Blue/Navy/light-neutral treatments now carry the visual system; semantic Green is reduced to small verified/success cues. Existing brand mark, monogram, responsive identity and dark-surface contrast remain intact.

Mobile-navigation integrity: the valid screenshot finding from the parallel v32.5.2 branch is absorbed under v34.1 rather than allowing an older api/index.js to bypass the governing brand layer. Server rendering, CSS and bounded client reconciliation now enforce exactly one semantic /decision-lab/ destination inside mobile navigation: the approved primary Decision Lab control, followed by Ask Scout. v34.1 deliberately uses no MutationObserver, preserving the v32.5.1 observer-loop stability principle.

Scout identity: Scout is a recognisable first-party character, not the superseded teal/yellow mascot and not a bare APG logo. The APG navigator uses APG Navy, APG Blue, white/light-blue and a restrained Teal highlight, with the APG master mark worn as a badge. The character is used in the floating launcher, panel avatar and conversational bot avatar. Consumer-facing wording is normalised to “Scout” and “Your APG decision guide”. The old “Shopping Assistant / Evidence-backed product matching” shell wording is superseded. Scout recommendation logic, structured-session continuity and zero-commercial-weight controls are unchanged.

Every-page HTML/text audit contract: exact-Production v34.1 certification reads the live sitemap and fetches every canonical route, requiring HTTP 200, the v34.1 presentation marker, a valid page title and main content, rejecting superseded Scout wording and requiring exactly one mobile-navigation Decision Lab destination in the server-rendered shell.

Every-page rendered colour audit contract: v34.1 then headless-renders every canonical route at a standard desktop viewport and inspects visible computed colour, background, border, fill, stroke, shadow and pseudo-element styles. Any visible use of the known historical green/cyan families or old Scout palette is a release failure. The same exhaustive pass fails true document-width overflow, browser page errors or superseded assistant wording on any canonical page.

Responsive and interactive visual contract: representative major page families are additionally rendered on desktop and mobile with screenshots, including home, search, category index/category, product, comparison, Decision Lab shell/results, guides, brands, retailers, My APG and trust/legal content. Dedicated interactive states open Scout and mobile navigation, require the v34.1 character in launcher/panel/conversation, require exactly one visible approved Decision Lab destination with Ask Scout following it, and reject the legacy mascot. Screenshots plus canonical HTML, rendered-style and visual audit JSON are retained as the release artefact.

Release discipline: GitHub main remains authoritative. This RELEASE file is part of the v34.1 implementation change itself, so the source record and implementation share one exact SHA. The release becomes CURRENT only after that exact SHA is READY in Vercel Production and the published APG v34.1 Brand Conformity Certification status is SUCCESS. Existing v27/v32/v32.5.1 gates remain additional regression controls.

Remaining external gaps: lawful genuine-product photography remains a separate rights/delivery programme where authorised exact-model imagery is unavailable. Hosted Supabase Auth settings outside the connected writable surface remain separate owner/admin configuration work unless subsequently verified. Formal trade mark clearance/registration is not claimed by this release.
